From: dArkOS RG52 Mini port
Subject: GL: no disk shader cache when the driver has no binary formats

Mali's libmali (g29p1) reports no program binary formats and takes no binary
back: glProgramBinary of its own GL_MALI_PROGRAM_BINARY_ARM output fails to
link. Every precompiled entry was thrown away, and each start rebuilt every
program the transferable cache listed, about 1.4 s each on the RG52 Mini (122
for one game: nearly three minutes on its logo). With no binary format the
disk cache is not used at all (nothing loaded, nothing written); shaders are
built when they are first needed.

diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_shader_manager.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_shader_manager.cpp
index f4cdc7b..5fa5ca7 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_shader_manager.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_opengl/gl_shader_manager.cpp
@@ -504,6 +504,17 @@ void ShaderProgramManager::LoadDiskCache(const std::atomic_bool& stop_loading,
                                          const VideoCore::DiskResourceLoadCallback& callback,
                                          bool accurate_mul) {
     auto& disk_cache = impl->disk_cache;
+    // dArkOS: Mali's libmali (g29p1) reports no program binary formats and takes no binary back
+    // (glProgramBinary of its own GL_MALI_PROGRAM_BINARY_ARM output fails to link), so every
+    // precompiled entry was thrown away and each start rebuilt every program the transferable cache
+    // listed, about 1.4 s each on the RG52 Mini: 122 programs of one game kept it on its logo for
+    // nearly three minutes. With no binary format the disk cache only costs that start; returning
+    // before LoadTransferable leaves it unused (IsUsable() needs tried_to_load), so nothing is
+    // written either, and shaders are built when they are first needed, as without the cache.
+    if (GetSupportedFormats().empty()) {
+        LOG_INFO(Render_OpenGL, "No program binary formats: the disk shader cache is not used");
+        return;
+    }
     const auto transferable = disk_cache.LoadTransferable();
     if (!transferable) {
         return;
